August 2026/07
Dear colleagues,

we would like to introduce the Sentinel Market Monitoring. This Group Strat=
egy product is developed as a follow-up to the Strategy Review 2026 and wil=
l focus on regular updates of monitored energy market parameters which are =
critical for the growth of our business.

The first release looks at a parameter which affects all our business segme=
nts: total electricity consumption. There is currently a significant discon=
nect between market outlooks that show strong growth to follow the energy t=
ransition and the actual recent and historic developments of consumption. S=
entinel took a closer look at the underlying drivers of total electricity c=
onsumption to better understand this disconnect.

Key results:


  1.  Market Outlooks suggest strong growth in German electricity consumpti=
on (3-4% CAGR until 2035) and are based on progressing electrification of h=
eat, transport & industry as well as data centers and electrolysis.
  2.  Sentinel View sees sufficient momentum in e-mobility, heat pumps and =
data centers. However, lagging developments in industrial electrification &=
 consumption and electrolysis results in trajectory on lower end (2.8% CAGR=
 until 2035) of Confidence Range.
  3.  Year-to-date (January to July 2026) electricity consumption is up yea=
r-on-year, indicating 2026 consumption to increase by ~1%. This points towa=
rds an increasing momentum (0.5% CAGR 2023 =96 2025), however is not yet su=
fficient to align with strong growth outlook.

Therefore, continued close monitoring will be required.

For more details, please refer to the slide deck (attached and here<https:/=
/compass.eon.com/sites/about-e-on-group/e-on-group-strategy-and-sustainabil=
ity/e-on-group-strategy/KnowledgeArticle/670057/v1-power-demand> on Compass=
).

The scope of Sentinel will expand over time, with additional market paramet=
er dashboards planned in future releases. The next update is scheduled for =
October 2026.


If you find this content valuable, please feel free to forward it to collea=
gues who may also find it useful. The following links can be used to be add=
